1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,388
A Microsoft AI Foundry, Snowflake and Databricks POC

2
00:00:14,588 --> 00:00:35,550
Side effects are mentioned where pharmacovigilance does not look

3
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:58,973
The clock starts when anyone in the company first hears of the case

4
00:00:59,173 --> 00:01:17,865
Two distinct jobs: did PV receive everything, and is there anything nobody passed on?

5
00:01:18,065 --> 00:01:43,339
Spontaneous or solicited changes what "reportable" means

6
00:01:43,539 --> 00:01:57,136
Re-read every record. Keep what PV never received.

7
00:01:57,336 --> 00:02:20,622
Step 1 · Screen: adverse event, special situation, or nothing for PV?

8
00:02:20,822 --> 00:02:45,592
Step 2 · Extract the case facts, every one with its quote

9
00:02:45,792 --> 00:03:03,787
Step 3 · Deterministic rules: no model decides a deadline

10
00:03:03,987 --> 00:03:33,852
Step 4 · Match: has pharmacovigilance already got this case?

11
00:03:34,052 --> 00:03:57,144
Why patient initials matter: 0.69 to 0.84 and 0.84 to 0.96

12
00:03:57,344 --> 00:04:19,225
Step 5 · A finding with a priority and a proposed intake package

13
00:04:19,425 --> 00:04:38,413
Step 6 · Reconcile what vendors sent against what PV received

14
00:04:38,613 --> 00:04:51,920
The reviewer works a prioritised queue

15
00:04:52,120 --> 00:05:13,756
Confirm day 0, choose the outcome, record the decision

16
00:05:13,956 --> 00:05:35,895
Three systems, one repository, everything deployed by script

17
00:05:36,095 --> 00:05:56,282
Nine schemas: sources, the safety database, results, review, audit

18
00:05:56,482 --> 00:06:13,679
The agent's credential can read four secure views and nothing else

19
00:06:13,879 --> 00:06:33,203
One Foundry project, two providers, no API keys

20
00:06:33,403 --> 00:06:53,086
The matching agent is a hosted agent in Foundry Agent Service

21
00:06:53,286 --> 00:07:14,438
Secrets never sit in the image: a project connection injects the agent's key at start

22
00:07:14,638 --> 00:07:37,485
The sweep runs unattended as a container job

23
00:07:37,685 --> 00:07:55,287
Source text is untrusted: read-only tools, validation twice, content filters

24
00:07:55,487 --> 00:08:14,751
The same platform on Azure Databricks: same tables, results copied, nothing recomputed

25
00:08:14,951 --> 00:08:25,970
Same numbers on both platforms

26
00:08:26,170 --> 00:08:59,250
One command creates Azure: Foundry, models, registry, identities, Key Vault, the job, the Databricks workspace

27
00:08:59,450 --> 00:09:28,899
Four commands build the data platform: keys, bootstrap, migrations, load, app

28
00:09:29,099 --> 00:09:50,053
Build the image, deploy the hosted agents, put the keys in Key Vault, start a sweep

29
00:09:50,253 --> 00:10:10,494
CI on every push; deployment is a manual workflow with OIDC and no stored secrets

30
00:10:10,694 --> 00:10:32,593
Develop and evaluate on a laptop: the same runner over a local file

31
00:10:32,793 --> 00:10:54,976
450 synthetic records with known answers, anchored on real cases

32
00:10:55,176 --> 00:11:09,529
Custom evaluators in Foundry grade routing, matching and causality

33
00:11:09,729 --> 00:11:28,916
Measured, not assumed

34
00:11:29,116 --> 00:11:43,602
What the numbers do not say

35
00:11:43,802 --> 00:12:01,564
From proof of concept to production

36
00:12:01,764 --> 00:12:39,994
Everything in the box

37
00:12:40,194 --> 00:12:54,356
github.com/cesarzea/pharmacovigilance-sweep
